A1 L1: with a world loaded, RM_WorldDecals.Probe finds the shipped test atlas World/Decals/RM_BlueDesert as 512x512 grid=2, Info shows the planet built with "decals: N glyphs on M flat tiles" and enabled=True, and the fade alpha in force equals the rule for the camera altitude in force (full <= decalFullAlt 380, gone >= decalGoneAlt 620), and Info's matAlpha (a live decal material's color.a) equals the same rule whenever a biome with an atlas is on the planet (no matAlpha in Info is a FAIL; no atlas biome on the planet is UNMEASURED, never PASS), so the per-frame material-alpha fade runs and reaches the material (N may be 0: a biome of ours on 0 tiles is expected).
